  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 46e4e4e1eba2d423bb36718521bc37fa, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q_1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "A customer says, \u201CCan I get something cold and sweet?\u201D Why
    might the AI still make the wrong prediction?"
  answers:
  - Because cold drinks cannot be predicted by AI.
  - Because sweet drinks are removed from the menu.
  - Because the coffee machine is disconnected.
  - Because the sentence could match several drinks.
  answerExplanation: "Words like \u201Ccold\u201D and \u201Csweet\u201D can describe
    many different drinks, so the AI must choose the most likely one."
  correctAnswer: 3
